body:
Assigning a Variant to a String will convert it to String, which is something all Variant types support. It's highly unlikely for this value to be something else than a String, unless users manually edited the file to write invalid values. In such a case the resulting String (e.g. stringification of `42` as `"42"`) will just not match any driver and shader baking will be skipped.

We don't normally do extra validation of the result of `GLOBAL_GET` or related functions, e.g.:
```
editor/editor_data.cpp
1085:           Dictionary d = GLOBAL_GET("_global_script_class_icons");

editor/export/editor_export_platform_pc.cpp
72:             String export_renderer = GLOBAL_GET("rendering/renderer/rendering_method");

modules/godot_physics_2d/register_types.cpp
40:     bool using_threads = GLOBAL_GET("physics/2d/run_on_separate_thread");
```

